// A call that SKIPS a defaulted parameter carries a supplied mask — one `u64`, shifted up by one on
// a method call to make room for the receiver at bit 0 — so such a call can only name parameters
// among the first 63. Naming one past that is E0061, at the call, naming the parameter that does
// not fit. Reordering is unaffected: a call filling a dense prefix carries no mask at any arity
// (`named_arguments_wide_arity.noe`).
//
// The call sits in a function nothing calls, so the rejection can only be the checker's: a program
// that reached its runtime would run to completion and print, and the `exit 1` below would fail.
// expect: error E0061 at 13:27
// expect: exit 1
